=== np_zap ===
Zap a wand in the given cardinal (n, e, s, w) or ordinal direction (ne, se, sw, nw) or target yourself using self.
  schema: {}

=== np_pickup ===
Pickup things at your location or specify where you want to pickup an item.
  schema: {}

=== np_up ===
Go up a staircase at your location or specify the position of the staircase you want to use.
  schema: {}

=== np_down ===
Go down a staircase at your location or specify the position of the staircase you want to use.
  schema: {}

=== np_loot ===
Loot a box on the floor.
  schema: {}

=== np_offer ===
Offer a sacrifice to the gods.
  schema: {}

=== np_drop ===
Drop an item.
  schema: {}

=== np_read ===
Read a scroll, spellbook, or something else.
  schema: {}

=== np_put_on ===
Put on an accessory.
  schema: {}

=== np_remove ===
Remove an accessory (ring, amulet, or blindfold).
  schema: {}

=== np_takeoff ===
Take off one piece of armor.
  schema: {}

=== np_wield ===
Wield a weapon.
  schema: {}

=== np_wear ===
Wear a piece of armor.
  schema: {}

=== np_apply ===
Apply (use) a tool. If used on a wand, that wand will be broken, releasing its magic in the process.
  schema: {}

=== np_eat ===
Eat something from your inventory or straight from the ground.
  schema: {}

=== np_drink ===
Drink something from your inventory or straight from the ground.
  schema: {}

=== np_tip ===
Tip out the content of a container.
  schema: {}

=== np_dip ===
Dip an object into something.
  schema: {}

=== np_kick ===
Kick something.
  schema: {}

=== np_rest ===
Rests n-moves while doing nothing or until something happens (default=5).
  schema: {}

=== np_cast ===
Opens your spellbook to cast a spell.
  schema: {}

=== np_pay ===
Pay your shopping bill.
  schema: {}

=== np_pray ===
Pray to the gods for help.
  schema: {}

=== np_look ===
Look at what is under you.
  schema: {}

=== np_set_avoid_monster_flag ===
If set to true skills will try to avoid monsters.
  schema: {}

=== np_melee_attack ===
Pursues and attacks a given target using melee attacks until it is dead.
  schema: {}

=== np_explore_level ===
Explores the level to find new rooms, as well as hidden doors and corridors.
  schema: {}

=== np_move_to ===
Move to the specified position using pathfinding.
  schema: {}

=== np_go_to ===
Moves to the specified room or corridor using the shortest path possible.
  schema: {}

=== np_press_key ===
Presses the given letter. For special keys only ESC, SPACE, and ENTER are supported.
  schema: {}

=== np_type_text ===
Types the text by pressing the keys in order.
  schema: {}

=== search ===
Search adjacent tiles for hidden passages and traps. Pass `times` to repeat — hidden passages typically need 5-10 searches at the same tile to reveal. Defaults to 1.
  schema: {}

=== reveal ===
Reveal a rectangular region of the dungeon map as ASCII (for the bounding-box observation mode, where the map is otherwise hidden). Coordinates are map cells: x = column 0-78, y = row 0-20, inclusive. The FULL map (x1=0, y1=0, x2=78, y2=20) is a valid request and returns all 79 columns. Returns the sub-rectangle as text; consumes NO game turn. Out-of-range requests are clamped to the grid, and any clamping is stated in the reply.
  schema: {}

